From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Taverley's portal was floating - move it to level ground

The footprint spread there was 32 and the check said so; it was placed anyway
because the spread of 4 the Rimmington round enforced had already been shown
to be one town's answer rather than a law, and Taverley had been looked at in
game. It floats. So 32 is past whatever the real limit is, and the number was
right this time.

There is nowhere level nearby that faces west. The ground in west Taverley
falls north-south, so a footprint five deep always spans the slope - the
nearest level west-facing site in the whole square is 48 tiles away. It has to
be an even angle, and it cannot sit on the road strip at z62-63 either: that
is overlay 10, three tiles wide, and a 5x2 that blocks would close it.

Moved to 17,57 facing south: x17-21, z57-58, every tile h48, spread 0, on the
open mud floor east of the buildings rather than on the road. Landing 19,56,
agent 20,56, both h48.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS; poh_mutate 93/93 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
